<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Starter feeds (D-hobby-feeds §7.1) — offered when a household's reader is
  empty, and never subscribed to on anybody's behalf. A blank paste field
  asks the user to already know what RSS is; this is a stocked shelf, not a
  recommendation engine, and every row is a checkbox somebody has to tick.

  What earns a place here, in priority order:

    1. a publisher-run URL. Never an aggregator or a FeedBurner proxy —
       a feed that lives on somebody else's redirector is the Google Reader
       failure mode this whole feature exists to answer;
    2. no account, no key, no paywall on the feed itself;
    3. a decade of URL stability, since this file ships in the repo and rots
       silently otherwise;
    4. politeness to poll, because this list multiplies by every self-hoster
       who ticks it;
    5. spread across the kinds of things people have hobbies about, rather
       than a news firehose.

  The folders are hobby names, which is what makes this work: Feeds::Opml
  matches a folder to an existing lens by name, so a household that already
  has a Cooking hobby files these on the way in, and the classifier
  (Feeds::Classify) handles the rest. The shelf is browsed a topic at a time
  (the groups render collapsed), so breadth costs the reader nothing — a
  folder nobody opens is one line of text.

  Verifying: script/check_starter_feeds.rb fetches every URL here and reports
  what moved, and .github/workflows/starter-feeds.yml runs it weekly and on
  every pull request that touches this file. A row that fails there is fixed
  or dropped — a starter that 404s in a brand-new account is worse than one
  we never offered.
-->
<opml version="2.0">
  <head>
    <title>Starter feeds</title>
  </head>
